# Detect the stack

- Read the tree, manifests, and tool configs before you name a language or a framework.
- Every language is in scope, including mixed repos. Open only the language skill that owns the file you are changing, and only the roles that match what you read.
- Name the repository type you actually see: application, library, monorepo, service, data pipeline, infrastructure, documentation, plugin, embedded, game, mobile, notebook, or empty template.
- Do not add a framework, package manager, or test runner that this repo does not already use.

```text
BAD:  This is a web app, so add a TypeScript page component.
GOOD: pyproject.toml and src/ own this change. Edit the Python package that already builds.
```
